{{#if (isMono)}}
Auth lives in `packages/auth`: `auth.ts` exports the `createAuth({{#if (has "database" "d1")}}db, {{/if}}cookiePlugin?)` factory and `type Auth`, `auth-client.ts` is the client. The factory contains no framework cookie plugin: it appends the one it receives after its own plugins, and the cookie plugin must stay last. `@repo/auth/auth` only exports the factory.
Add a social provider by editing `socialProviders` in `packages/auth/src/auth.ts`.
{{else}}
Auth config in `src/lib/auth/`. `create-auth.ts` exports the `createAuth({{#if (has "database" "d1")}}db, {{/if}}cookiePlugin?)` factory and `type Auth`, `auth-client.ts` is the client. The factory appends the cookie plugin it receives after its own plugins, and the cookie plugin must stay last.
Add a social provider by editing `socialProviders` in `create-auth.ts`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "database" "d1")}}
{{#if (eq stackName "nextjs")}}
`getAuth()` in `src/lib/server.ts` builds this app's instance per request with `{{> better-auth/cookie-plugin}}`: call it, never build one yourself.
{{else}}
`src/lib/server.ts` builds this app's `auth` once at module scope with `createAuth(db, {{> better-auth/cookie-plugin}})`: import it from there.
{{/if}}
{{else}}
`src/lib/auth/auth.ts` exports this app's `auth`, built from the factory with `{{> better-auth/cookie-plugin}}`: import it from there.
{{/if}}
Without a cookie plugin the factory disables session refresh: a refresh through an instance that cannot forward cookies would extend the session in the database but not in the browser.
{{#if (has "deployment" "cloudflare")}}
Rate limiting keys on the client address read from `cf-connecting-ip` (`advanced.ipAddress.ipAddressHeaders` in the factory). Cloudflare sets it on every request and a client cannot choose it. A request without it (a local run outside the Cloudflare edge) falls into one shared bucket.
{{else}}
Rate limiting keys on the client address read from `x-forwarded-for` (`advanced.ipAddress.ipAddressHeaders` in the factory, {{#if (isMono)}}`packages/auth/src/auth.ts`{{else}}`src/lib/auth/create-auth.ts`{{/if}}). Better-auth trusts only a single-value header: a header carrying several addresses is rejected and the request falls into one shared `no-trusted-ip` bucket. What that means depends on what sits in front of the app:
- **No proxy (the app is exposed directly, for example `next start` or Nitro)**: any client can send a different `x-forwarded-for` on every request and is never rate limited, so password guesses are unlimited. The app must sit behind a reverse proxy or CDN that overwrites the header with the real client address.
- **One proxy that appends (nginx `$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`, an ALB, CloudFront)**: safe. A client-supplied value turns the header into several addresses, which better-auth rejects, so a spoofing client lands in the shared bucket instead of escaping the limit.
- **A chain of proxies (a CDN, then a load balancer)**: every legitimate request carries several addresses, so all clients share the `no-trusted-ip` bucket and one client can make every sign-in answer 429. Set `advanced.ipAddress.trustedProxies` next to `ipAddressHeaders` in the factory to the addresses or CIDR ranges of your own proxies (`trustedProxies: ['192.0.2.10', '10.0.0.0/24']`): better-auth then walks the header from the right, skips them, and keys on the first untrusted address. Never list a range that also covers clients.
If the platform in front of the app sets another header, put that one in `ipAddressHeaders`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (hasLibrary "trpc")}}
The tRPC notes say which instance the tRPC context reads the session through, and whether that read extends the session.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq stackName "tanstack-start")}}

**TanStack Start**
- `src/routes/api/auth/$.ts` serves every `/api/auth/*` request through `auth.handler`.
- `{{> better-auth/cookie-plugin}}` is the cookie plugin of this app's instance and stays last in the plugins: it forwards the cookies set by auth calls made from server functions.
- `getSession` (`src/lib/auth/session.ts`) is a server function returning the current session or `null`. Call it from a route `beforeLoad` or `loader`. No protected layout is generated: guard routes yourself.
- Per-request session cache: `getRequestSession(headers, load)` ({{#if (isMono)}}`@repo/auth/session-cache`{{else}}`src/lib/auth/session-cache.ts`{{/if}}) memoizes the session **promise** in a `WeakMap<Headers, Promise<Session | null>>`. Loaders and server functions running in the same SSR request share one lookup, even when they start concurrently: the cache key is `request.headers`, the same `Headers` object for the whole request. Read the session through it (as `getSession` does), not with `auth.api.getSession` directly.
{{#if (has "database" "d1")}}
- Cloudflare + D1: `auth` is built once at module scope, never per request. Locally `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` and `BETTER_AUTH_URL` come from `.env`; `vite build` snapshots `.env` into `dist/server/.dev.vars`, which `vite preview` reads, so rebuild after editing it.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
